<mxCell id="note" value="U = LN1(X); O = Attention(U); R = QACT(X + O); V = LN2(R); F = FFN(V); next X = QACT(R + F).&lt;br&gt;LN1 and LN2 reuse one engine with different learned gamma/beta. Residual additions reuse one element-wise controller.&lt;br&gt;Original X is preserved through attention; R is preserved through FFN. No inference dropout." style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#374151;fontColor=#374151;strokeWidth=2;rounded=0;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontColor=#263442;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="615" width="1440" height="85" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
