<mxCell id="note" value="A = QACT(W1·V[t] + b1); G = GELU(A); F[t] = QACT(W2·G + b2). D is token width; 4D is hidden width.&lt;br&gt;Python nn.GELU() targets x·Φ(x), with Φ(x) = ½[1+erf(x/√2)]. Method, range and accuracy are still open.&lt;br&gt;No inference dropout. Residual R is not stored in FFN scratch and cannot be overwritten by these calculations." style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#374151;fontColor=#374151;strokeWidth=2;rounded=0;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontColor=#263442;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="615" width="1440" height="85" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
